content.text:
## Summary of the empirical finding first (it pins the bug)

I inspected the live machine state, which makes the diagnosis concrete:

- `C:\Users\Victor\AppData\Local\entire\plugins\pkg\graph\entire-graph.exe` — **75,255,808 bytes, intact**, created 11/09/2026 09:09:30.
- `...\pkg\graph\manifest.yml` — `tag: v0.4.0`, `asset: entire-graph_0.4.0_windows_arm64.zip`, `sha256`, `binary_sha256` all recorded (so download → checksum verify → zip extract → `pkg/` placement all worked on windows/arm64).
- `...\plugins\bin\` — currently empty only because the shell history shows `rm ...\bin\entire-graph.exe` was run manually. So `bin\entire-graph.exe` **did** get created.
- `whoami /priv`: `SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege` is **present but Disabled** in the token (this shell also holds `SeDebugPrivilege`/`SeRestorePrivilege` → admin token). Developer Mode is off (`HKLM\...\AppModelUnlock` exists with **no values**).
- Go 1.27.1 windows-arm64 toolchain: `os.Root.Symlink` → `internal/syscall/windows.Symlinkat` wraps the call in **`withPrivilege("SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege", …)`**, which does `ImpersonateSelf` + `AdjustTokenPrivileges(SE_PRIVILEGE_ENABLED)` (`at_windows.go:502-511`, `618-653`). A token that *has* the privilege disabled therefore gets it enabled, and **the symlink succeeds**.

⇒ On Windows the `bin/` entry is created by the **symlink branch**, so `bin\entire-graph.exe` is a reparse point. `dir`/`Get-ChildItem` report a Windows symlink's own length as **0 bytes** — that is the "EMPTY binary". The real payload is the 75 MB file in `pkg\graph\`.

Second, independent defect found while tracing: the documented "symlink → hardlink → copy" ladder is really "symlink → *always fails* → copy", because `os.Root.Link` resolves **both** operands inside the root (`$GOROOT/src/os/root_openat.go:277-293` calls `doInRoot(r, oldname, …)`), and `src` is an absolute path outside the root (`splitPathInRoot`, `$GOROOT/src/os/root.go:301-307`, plus `rootCleanPath` on Windows, reject it with `errPathEscapes`). So the hardlink fallback that exists *specifically for Windows* can never fire.

---

## 1. Files implementing plugin install/download

All under `C:\Users\Victor\cli\cmd\entire\cli\`:

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `plugin.go` (296 ln) | kubectl dispatcher, `MaybeRunPlugin`, `resolvePlugin`, `runPlugin` |
| `plugin_on_demand.go` (160 ln) | `installMissingPlugin` — the `entire graph` prompt path |
| `plugin_store.go` (639 ln) | `pluginParentDir`, `pluginRoot`, `PluginBinDir`, `InstallPluginFromPath`, `materializeManagedEntry`, `copyFileStreaming` |
| `plugin_fetch.go` (774 ln) | asset candidates, checksums, `downloadPluginAsset`, `fetchAndVerify`, `extractPluginBinary`, tar.gz/zip extraction, **`writeExecutableLimited`** |
| `plugin_install_remote.go` (397 ln) | `InstallPluginFromRepo`, `installRepoAtTag`, **`replaceBinary`**, `oldBinaryAsideName`, `sweepOldBinaries` |
| `plugin_manifest.go` (374 ln) | `windowsExeExt`, `pluginBinaryName`, `PluginManifest`, `PluginMetadata`, pkg dir |
| `plugin_index.go` (356 ln) | git-cloned index repo, `index.json` |
| `plugin_gitremote.go`, `plugin_deps.go`, `plugin_group.go`, `plugin_confirm.go`, `plugin_progress.go`, `plugin_env.go`, `plugin_official.go` | tags/metadata, deps, cobra commands, prompt, spinner, env, allowlist |
| `jsonutil/write.go` | `CreateTempIn`, `WriteFileAtomic`, `WriteFileAtomicIn` |
| `osroot/osroot.go` | `Shared`, `Forget`, `MkdirAllNoSymlink`, `ReadDirNoSymlinks`, `RemoveNoSymlinks`, `WriteFile` |
| `internal/entireclient/userdirs/userdirs.go` | `RequireAbsoluteOverride` for `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR` |

Note: **there is no `_windows_test.go` anywhere in the plugin code.** The only Windows-tagged plugin source file is `plugin_signal_windows.go` (14 ln, signal stub).

---

## 2. Full path from `entire graph` to the binary on disk

### a. Dispatch (`cmd/entire/main.go`, `plugin.go`)

`main.go:81` → `cli.PrependPluginBinDirToPATH(ctx)` prepends `%LOCALAPPDATA%\entire\plugins\bin`.
`main.go:83` → `cli.MaybeRunPlugin(ctx, rootCmd, os.Args[1:])`.

`plugin.go:152-190` `resolvePlugin`: built-ins win; then `exec.LookPath("entire-graph")`. On `exec.ErrNotFound` **and** `name == onDemandInstallPluginName` (`plugin.go:43`, `= "graph"`) it returns `binPath == ""` to signal "offer install".

`plugin.go:84-115` → `installMissingPlugin` → on success prints `Running entire-graph`, then `runPlugin` (`plugin.go:240`).

### b. Prompt (`plugin_on_demand.go:18-129`)

