## 3. Asset selection / index

**Index** (`plugin_index.go:28-51`): a **git clone of an index repository**, not a REST API.
- `defaultPluginIndexURL = "https://github.com/entireio/plugin-index"`, override `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_INDEX_URL` or `--index`.
- File at repo root: `index.json`, schema version 1, shallow clone cached in the user cache dir, TTL 24 h, marker `.entire-last-sync`, cap 8 MiB.
- Entry shape (`plugin_index.go:64-72`): `{name, repo_url, description, official, platforms[]}`. **No asset/URL/checksum data lives in the index** — it only maps name → repo URL.
- There is **no `testdata/` directory for the plugin index**; tests build index repos inline (`plugin_index_test.go`, `plugin_on_demand_test.go:74`, `integration_test/plugin_remote_install_test.go`).

**Per-repo metadata**: `entire-plugin.yml` at the repo root (`plugin_manifest.go:154-174`) — optional `name`, `description`, `download_url` template (`{name} {tag} {version} {os} {arch} {asset}`), `requires`.

**Asset naming / zip-vs-tar.gz decision** (`plugin_fetch.go:154-214`):

```go
func assetCandidates(name, tag string) []string {
	binName := pluginBinaryPrefix + name
	version := strings.TrimPrefix(tag, "v")
	stems := make([]string, 0, 16)
	for _, osName := range osAliases(runtime.GOOS) {          // darwin -> {darwin, macos}
		for _, arch := range platformArchAliases(runtime.GOOS, runtime.GOARCH) {
			stems = append(stems,
				fmt.Sprintf("%s_%s_%s_%s", binName, version, osName, arch),
				fmt.Sprintf("%s_%s_%s", binName, osName, arch),
			)
		}
	}
	exts := []string{".tar.gz", ".zip", ""}
	if runtime.GOOS == windowsGOOS {
		exts = []string{".zip", ".tar.gz", windowsExeExt}
	}
	var out []string
	for _, ext := range exts {
		for _, stem := range stems {
			out = append(out, stem+ext)
		}
	}
	return out
}
```

`archAliases` (`:155-164`): `amd64 → {amd64, x86_64}`, `arm64 → {arm64, aarch64}`. **No amd64 fallback for windows/arm64** — an arm64 host will not accept a `windows_amd64` asset. Here it did not matter: the release publishes `entire-graph_0.4.0_windows_arm64.zip` and that is what the manifest records.

Format dispatch is by filename suffix only (`plugin_fetch.go:492-508`):

```go
func extractPluginBinary(assetPath, name string, destRoot *os.Root, destName string) error {
	binName := pluginBinaryPrefix + name
	lower := strings.ToLower(assetPath)
	switch {
	case strings.HasSuffix(lower, ".tar.gz") || strings.HasSuffix(lower, ".tgz"):
		return extractFromTarGz(assetPath, binName, destRoot, destName)
	case strings.HasSuffix(lower, ".zip"):
		return extractFromZip(assetPath, binName, destRoot, destName)
	default:
		src, err := os.Open(assetPath)
		...
		return writeExecutable(destRoot, destName, src)
	}
}
```

Entry matching tolerates `.exe` on Windows (`:512-518`), selection is shallowest-path-then-lexicographic (`archiveEntryPicker`, `:558-573`). `extractFromZip` (`:668-698`) ends in `writeExecutable(destRoot, destName, rc)`.

**Checksums**: `checksumsFileName = "checksums.txt"` plus `<bin>_<ver>_checksums.txt` / `<bin>_checksums.txt` (`:218-229`); `selectAssetFromChecksums` (`:249-256`) picks the first `assetCandidates` entry present in the manifest; `fetchAndVerify` (`:419-486`) streams SHA-256 while writing into the staging root via `stagingRoot.Create(asset)` and deletes the partial on mismatch. Unverified installs are refused unless `--allow-unverified`.

